speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, pursuant to the provisions of Standing Order 43, I request the unanimous consent of the House to move a motion.
In view of the fact that in the announcement made recently by the Canadian Dairy Commission concerning dairy policies for 1974, there is no guarantee of a required minimum income for dairy producers; that the Quebec Federation of Industrial Milk Producers has decided, at its annual assembly yesterday, to implement a plan of action aiming at withholding dairy products, and that the precarious situation in which the Canadian egg producers find themselves is due to the import of American eggs on the Canadian market, I move, seconded by the hon. member for Saint-Hyacinthe (Mr. Wagner);
That the responsible committee of the House do convene immediately to discuss these problems in order that new recommendations may be put by this committee to the House so as to solve the problems that these two categories of producers are now facing.

Agreed.
Motion withdrawn.
;
